      {
        "finding": "For CIFAR-100 ResNet50, largest Hessian eigenvalues are 26 ± 2, 21 ± 3, and 18 ± 1 for vanilla, SAM, and mSAM; for WRN-28-10 they are 92 ± 4, 30 ± 2, and 17 ± 1. Within each architecture, lower eigenvalues accompany higher test accuracy.",
        "proposed_claim": "Across these three training methods within each of two CIFAR-100 CNN architectures, lower unscaled Hessian eigenvalues accompany better held-out accuracy.",
        "row_ids": [
          "R7",
