    "peer_reviewed": "OPT2022: 14th Annual Workshop on Optimization for Machine Learning",
    "problems": "The study does not measure training error or a training-test gap. The sharpness analysis uses largest Hessian eigenvalue, not the magnitude-aware measure in V7, and reports only two CNNs on CIFAR 100. Results are task- and method-specific; the authors note comparably high run variance for smaller NLP datasets such as COLA and MRPC.",
    "rows_left_out": "No extracted accuracy rows were omitted. Runtime values in Appendix A were left out because runtime is not an outcome named by the claim versions. Hybrid-training figure results were left out because they concern a training-efficiency tradeoff and do not measure a listed version.",
